# Searchlight: turns a cone of light on the nearest enemy unit in range. Every enemy in the cone is solid (as in a
# lantern field) and burns. It draws light only while it shines ("Searchlight light/s").
# Spawned origin 2.0 above ground.
# SHAPE (a placeholder; uniform scales of the baseshapes variants): a dark IRON MAST on a foot (the root) - a thin post
# of two pieces (1.8 m each, overlapping by 0.1 m), a lamp deck turned 45 degrees, a warm yellow lamp 5.4 m over the
# ground and a roof over it. It reads against the Light tower's pale stone obelisk with its blue crystal. The child
# pieces are render-only; the collider is the 4x4x4 m box. The cone itself is a spot light the game adds each frame
# from the lamp (keep the `Lamp` height in step with c_searchlightLamp in Game/Private/Light.cpp). The deck and the
# roof are narrow on purpose: the light starts 1 m in front of the lamp and must clear them.
Prefab gameSearchlight
	Global true
	Component Render
		ObjectContainer baseshapes
		Node CubeHalf
		Type StaticMesh
		Color 0.22 0.23 0.27
		Position 0 -1.3 0
		Scale 1.4
	Component Physics
		Body Static
		ContactEvents true
		Shape Box
		HalfExtents 2 2 2
	Component GameStructure
		AlwaysShowResources true
		MeleeRadius 2
	Component Scene
		Entity
			Name Post
			Position 0 0.3 0
			Component Render
				ObjectContainer baseshapes
				Node Pillar3
				Type StaticMesh
				Color 0.3 0.3 0.34
				Scale 0.3
		Entity
			Name Post2
			Position 0 2.0 0
			Component Render
				ObjectContainer baseshapes
				Node Pillar3
				Type StaticMesh
				Color 0.3 0.3 0.34
				Scale 0.3
		Entity
			Name Deck
			Position 0 2.9 0
			Component Render
				ObjectContainer baseshapes
				Node CubeQuarter
				Type StaticMesh
				Color 0.22 0.23 0.27
				Rotation 0 45 0
				Scale 0.5
		Entity
